    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "opening": "# Verifiable Practice\n\nVerifiable Practice\u2014VP\u2014is a vendor-neutral framework for making AI-assisted software work inspectable, falsifiable, and evidence-led. It treats plausible output as a hypothesis, not a result: clarify the goal, state what would disprove a claim, seek counterexamples, and report the evidence\u2014including failures.\n\nFor the motivation and a worked example, read [Why Verifiable Practice](WHY.md).\n\nThe repository itself is a reusable AI skill. [SKILL.md](SKILL.md) contains the operating rules and routes an assistant to the relevant concepts and playbooks without loading the entire framework into context.\n\nThis repository has adopted prospective record keeping under the\n[current project charter](vp/PROJECT.md). Its [operational records](vp/README.md)",
      "identity_present": false
    },
    {
      "path": "WHY.md",
      "opening": "# Why Verifiable Practice\n\nSoftware work with AI should be designed so that another person or system can check its goals, claims, decisions, and results. That is Verifiable Practice.\n\nBullshit is not lying. Liars know the truth and conceal it. Bullshitters are indifferent to truth. They say what sounds right, what fits the meeting, what satisfies the prompt. Whether it happens to be true is incidental.\n\nSoftware engineering is drowning in bullshit. \"Best practice\" that nobody tested. Architecture decisions justified by vibes. AI-generated code that looks correct and compiles and passes the obvious tests and fails in production.\n\nVP is a framework for not doing that.\n",
      "identity_present": false
    },
    {
      "path": "SKILL.md",
      "opening": "\n\n# Verifiable Practice\n\nWhen working on this repository itself, read its [record root](vp/README.md)\nand [current state](vp/STATE.md). Its prospective charter governs tracking;\nlegacy history is not certified and a conformance claim needs independent A.\nThese repository-specific links do not enrol another project using this skill.\n\nTreat every material claim as something that must be possible to check. Establish what the user is trying to achieve, identify what would show the current approach is wrong, seek that evidence, and report the observed result\u2014including failures and uncertainty.",
      "identity_present": false
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/how-vp-works.md",
      "opening": "# How Verifiable Practice Works\n\nAI systems produce plausible language quickly. Plausibility is useful for generating possibilities, but it is not evidence that a claim is true or that software meets its goal. VP externalises the discipline needed to close that gap.\n\n## The Failure Modes\n\n| Failure mode | What happens |\n|--------------|--------------|\n| Goal drift | Work optimises an intermediate task while the desired outcome disappears from view |\n| Confirmation bias | Checks demonstrate familiar examples but do not challenge the claim |",
      "identity_present": false
    }
  ],
